meta {
  name: admin
  seq: 4
}

docs {
  Outbox/dead-letter triage, the live request feed, and the audit log.
  Every request here requires an admin token and its own permission
  (messaging:read, requests:read or audit:read); system_admin holds all
  three, so one token covers the folder. Outbox status and the DLQ list
  answer meaningfully on a fresh database: the outbox table is empty rather
  than absent, so status reads all zeros and the DLQ list is [].

  There is no "replay" request in this folder. Replay needs an existing
  dead letter, and nothing in this collection can produce one — a message
  only reaches the DLQ after a consumer exhausts its retries, which is not
  a thing an HTTP client can trigger on demand. The one replay case this
  collection can exercise honestly is "the id does not exist", and that
  lives in errors/ next to the rest of the 404s.
}
